[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   Step 091 -- inner-perturber ('Planet Y') ladder: required mass at
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   a = 100-200 AU vs the ephemeris bound
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   Siraj, Chyba & Tremaine (2025) showed that the distant-belt mean-plane
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   warp cannot be generated by either published distant-planet
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   realization and would instead require a THIRD body -- 'Planet Y' --
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   of roughly Mercury-to-Earth mass (0.06-1 M_earth) at a = 100-200 AU
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   with i >~ 10 deg.  Steps 083/087 measured the required point mass for
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   distant rungs (a9 = 250-1000 AU) on the cometary boundary-rotation
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   channel; this step extends the ladder INWARD into the Planet-Y regime
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   and asks two questions:
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   (i)  Can an inner perturber in the SCT25 parameter range produce
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   the observed boundary rotation delta theta at all?  The
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   required mass is measured on the same CODE class-1 sample with
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   the same IAS15/DE440s machinery and the linear mass scaling
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   verified in step 083.
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   (ii) Is that required mass compatible with the planetary-ephemeris
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   bound?  Gomes, Murray, Gomes, Holman & Bernstein (2023, PSJ
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   4:66) forecast a median tidal-field uncertainty
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   sigma_M = 0.22 M_earth (d/400 AU)^3
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   from Juno/Cassini/Mars ranging; the 5-sigma detection line
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   1.1 M_earth (d/400 AU)^3 is the boundary above which an inner
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   perturber should already appear in the ephemerides.
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   Two perturber geometries are integrated per rung:
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   'anti-aligned' -- the BB21 shepherding orientation continued inward
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   (e9=0.30, i9=15.6 deg, varpi9=246.7 deg, Om9=96.9 deg), so the
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   100-200 AU rungs join continuously onto the step-087 ladder.
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   'warp-plane' -- a perturber sharing the measured warp plane
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   (i9=15 deg, Om9=120 deg; step 090 / SCT25), with varpi9=229 deg
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   antipodal to the lambda=49 deg boundary axis -- the orientation
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   that leans the disk toward the observed cap.
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   Rungs: a9 = 100, 125, 150, 175, 200, 250 AU.  Deliverables per rung
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   and geometry: the injected rotation under 6.9 M_earth, the required-
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   mass distribution in/out of the theta<60 deg cap, and the margin
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   against the SCT25 Planet-Y box and the Gomes+23 5-sigma ephemeris
[2026-09-20 12:06:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 091]   line.
